<title>GERMANY: Buba's Welteke - Revaluation would hurt public faith.</title>
<headline>Buba's Welteke - Revaluation would hurt public faith.</headline>
<dateline>MAINZ, Germany 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Monday Bonn's plans to revalue the central bank's assets would damage public confidence in the central bank's monetary policy.</p>
<p>In an interview on German television, Welteke said it would amount to a &quot;giving of credit&quot; to the federal government if Germany's under-valued gold and currency reserves were to be priced at higher levels.</p>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel proposed more than two weeks ago to revalue the Bundesbank's official reserves at higher levels than they are now, increasing the central bank's profits which could be used to pay down government debt.</p>
<p>German television station ZDF provided a summary of Welteke's remarks in advance of when the interview was to air.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
